---
# ansible-lint gate. The CI workflow pins ansible-lint==26.6.0 for reproducibility.
#
# Enforced at the strictest built-in profile (production) with a single documented
# waiver:
#
#   var-naming[no-role-prefix] — requires every role variable to carry the role
#   name as a prefix (e.g. paperless_dbuser -> paperless_env_dbuser). For a private
#   single-tenant homelab repo this anti-collision guarantee has negligible value:
#   the roles are never shared to Galaxy, the variables are already semantically
#   namespaced (paperless_*, pg_backup_*), and the mandated prefixes are verbose and
#   redundant. This is a commonly-disabled rule; every other production-profile rule
#   (fqcn, risky-file-permissions, no-changed-when, name, role-name, yaml, ...) stays on.
profile: production
skip_list:
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
